From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: make the user documentation optional

gnome.yelp() runs itstool to merge translations into the help pages, and
subdir('help') is unconditional, so configure stops on a build that has no
itstool:

  help/meson.build:34:6: ERROR: Program 'itstool' not found or not executable

Add a help option, defaulting to true so nothing changes for anyone building
normally, and skip the subdir when it is off.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -8,3 +8,4 @@
 option('gci', type: 'boolean', value: true, description: 'Build GCalc UI library')
 option('app', type: 'boolean', value: true, description: 'Build GNOME Calculator Application')
 option('doc', type: 'boolean', value: true, description: 'Build GCalc and/or GCi documentation')
+option('help', type: 'boolean', value: true, description: 'Build the user documentation with yelp (needs itstool)')
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -109,9 +109,11 @@
 subdir('lib')
 subdir('src')
 subdir('search-provider')
+if get_option('help')
 subdir('help')
 endif
 endif
+endif
 
 if get_option('doc')
 subdir('doc')
